  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). No transitive pair.\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing rising or completed rise. {日|ひ}が{昇|のぼ}っている = 'the sun has risen / is rising.'\n\nWRITING:\nThree kanji are used for のぼる, each with a different meaning:\n- {昇|のぼ}る: natural rising (sun, moon) — this entry\n- {登|のぼ}る: climbing (mountains, stairs)\n- {上|のぼ}る: going up (general upward movement)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {日|ひ}が{昇|のぼ}る: the sun rises\n- {太陽|たいよう}が{昇|のぼ}る: the sun rises\n- {月|つき}が{昇|のぼ}る: the moon rises\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {登|のぼ}る: to climb (physical climbing)\n- {上|のぼ}る: to go up (general)\n- {上|あ}がる: to rise, to go up",
